# Project Plan Foundation: RCHN Patient Intake and Scheduling System
**Consultant:** Marcos Lara
**Role:** Associate Consultant, Project Manager, NovaTech Consulting
**Engagement:** Riverside Community Health Network (RCHN)
**Date:** September 24, 2026
---
## Scope
### In Scope, Phase One
Patient intake workflow standardization across all six clinics
Appointment scheduling system replacement
Staff training for the new system at all six locations
Initial rollout support for 90 days post-launch
Executive reporting dashboard for clinic leadership
### Out of Scope, Phase One
Billing system integration with the new scheduling data
Patient-facing online scheduling portal
Mobile application for clinic staff

### Scope Justification
One item that I mark outside of the scope is mobile application for clinic staff. The main test is whether or not it serves the business needs. The charter focus is replacing the RCHN intake and scheduling system. I am able to test whether a scope is included or excluded by asking if it helps the intake or scheduling work. Mobile application for the clinic staff does not help clinic intake complete intake and scheduling more consistently and reliability across the 6 clinics. Including items outside of the scope can redirect the project outcome. Including an application can bring in new users into the project, swaying away the attention from the clinic. It can also affect the schedule of the project, extending the milestones or deadlines. The cost of including more features can go against the budget from the sponsor.
## SMART Objectives
### Objective 1
Reducing the check in time for patients at all 6 RCHN clinics from 12 to 6 minutes when the project goes live.
**Connection to Product Vision:** it will mitigate the inconsistent work flows and re entries that have conflict with intake staff.

### Objective 2
Reduce double booked appointments across all 6 clinics by delivering conflict free booking And an on screen confirmation save for every appointment.
**Connection to Product Vision:** it will fix the problem of not knowing if the appointment was saved and the problem of the double booking of patients.

