## Planning Constraints
### Constraint 1
The first constraint is the intake and scheduling system, and data migration must comply with the HIPPA. This is non-negotiable.
**Effect on Planning:** Raising the cost to meet HIPPA expectations, having the inspectors to review and inspection that meet protocols it also expands the scope of the project. Involving stakeholders to secure data migration and access logging

### Constraint 2
a fixed rollout date for the project deployment
**Effect on Planning:** Having a fixed deadline will hold the project holders against a time of completed work they must deliver their work. This can raise the cost if stakeholders are behind on work or need extra time to complete the work. It also creates a risk in extending the project's time and affecting other areas.
