## Planning Foundation Synthesis
One planning decision that I made this week was the scope limit.  A patient self scheduling application is out of scope for the RCHN project. This was helpful as it made clarity of the staff intake and scheduling system. Using our week 2 charter helped highlight that patient portal and self scheduling as outside of the scope. The RCHN intake, scheduling, data migration, and training, and rollout support are items that would be included. Week 3 has also helped me understand that the product vision or the primary user as the clinic are the intake coordinator and not the patients. Intake coordinator needs are having a consistent workflow, clear save confirmation of the appointments, less reentry. Having an application for self searching will serve the project off track and solve a problem that isn't in the product charter
